{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"linear-paganist-elver","creation_channel":"cli","description":"# A PASS `COMPLETION_VERDICT` sidecar is silently lost on write-lock contention (exit 0, no stderr)\n\n## Observed\n\nClosing `d582-fd5a-7ece-4c32` (`--class flaky`) emitted a traceback ending in\n`flock: could not acquire lock after 60s`, yet **exited 0** and closed and certified the ticket\ncorrectly. The ticket is now missing its `*-COMPLETION_VERDICT.json` record. 810 tickets in this store\ncarry one; d582 does not.\n\nThe failing call is the PASS sidecar:\n\n* `llm/completion_sidecar.py:60` — `append_event(...)` inside `emit()` (defined `:47`)\n* called from `_commands/close_precheck.py:324` (the PASS branch; FAIL is `:310`)\n* raised at `_commands/_seam.py:419`, translating `LockTimeout` from `_store/lock.py:103`\n  (60s = `_DEFAULT_TIMEOUT` 30 x `_DEFAULT_ATTEMPTS` 2, `lock.py:73-74`)\n\n**It fires BEFORE the close, not after.** `close_precheck.py:324` runs inside `_completion_precheck`,\nwhich `transition_close.py:326` calls *before* `txn.transition_core(...)` at `:343` — the documented\nverify -> close -> sign order (`transition_close.py:246-252`). The STATUS and SIGNATURE writes then\nsucceeded seconds later (12:30:56 and 12:30:58), which is what makes the loss avoidable.\n\n## Why it is silent — the failure is swallowed twice\n\n`completion_sidecar.py:61-65` catches everything and returns `False`:\n\n```python\nexcept Exception:  # best-effort observability sidecar\n    logger.warning(\"COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecar emit failed; continuing\", exc_info=True)\n    return False\n```\n\nand the caller **discards that return value** — `close_precheck.py:322-326` wraps the call in a second\ntry/except and never inspects it.\n\nBest-effort is the correct POLICY: a sidecar must never fail a close. The defect is that a\n**transient, retryable** failure is handled identically to a permanent one:\n\n1. **No retry on `LockTimeout`.** One 60s attempt. Every subsequent close-path write succeeded within\n   seconds. A single re-attempt, or routing the sidecar through the same lock window as\n   STATUS+SIGNATURE (the `_batch_sink` seam already exists at `_seam.py:405-409`), saves the record.\n2. **No machine-readable signal.** Exit stays 0, stdout is clean, and this goes only through\n   `logger.warning` — unlike the drift and `SigningError` paths, which write explicit\n   `Warning: closed <id> WITHOUT ...` lines to stderr (`transition_close.py:387-393`, `:404-410`).\n   A `gate_error_sidecar` module exists (`llm/gate_error_sidecar.py:34` maps `\"completion\" ->\n   \"COMPLETION_VERDICT\"`) and is not engaged here.\n\n## Blast radius: metric skew, not state corruption\n\n`COMPLETION_VERDICT` is deliberately **reducer-ignored** (`completion_sidecar.py:11-16`,\n`reducer/_version.py:78`, `verify_authorship.py:378`), so compiled state, deps, validity and the\nattestation are all unaffected — d582 is correctly closed and certified, and **no remediation is\nneeded for it**. The durable cost is observability:\n\n* `metrics/sidecar_metrics.py:221` counts a ticket into the `first_pass_verification` denominator only\n  if it has a `COMPLETION_VERDICT` record;\n* `sidecar_metrics.py:106-110` counts accepted closes from `completion_verifier_pass_v1` records.\n\nd582 silently drops out of both. The record is also **not re-emittable** — the verdict dict was\nin-memory, so recovering it would need reopen -> re-close and a fresh billable verifier run.\n\n## Not a rare race — see the amplifier\n\nUnder parallel-agent load the 60s budget is routinely exceeded, so expect silent metric drift across\nmany closes rather than one. The amplifier is filed separately: compact-on-close holds the store write\nlock for minutes.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] a `LockTimeout` on the PASS/FAIL sidecar is RETRIED at least once, or the sidecar write is routed\n      into the same lock window as STATUS+SIGNATURE via the existing `_batch_sink` seam\n- [ ] when the sidecar is ultimately dropped, the close writes an explicit stderr warning naming the\n      ticket and what was lost, matching the existing `Warning: closed <id> WITHOUT ...` convention\n- [ ] `close_precheck` stops discarding `completion_sidecar.emit`'s boolean return\n- [ ] a test proves a sidecar `LockTimeout` no longer loses the record silently: it either lands after\n      retry, or a stderr warning is emitted — asserted, with the lock held by the test\n- [ ] the close still succeeds and stays certified when the sidecar genuinely cannot be written\n      (best-effort policy preserved, verified by a test that makes the write fail permanently)\n\n## Testing\n\n    pytest tests/unit -k \"sidecar or completion_verdict or lock\" -q\n    make lint && make typecheck","id":"ab54-f19f-d5bd-422c","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"PASS COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecar silently lost on write-lock contention (exit 0, no stderr)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785872464709258001,"uuid":"94b324ac-e911-4291-bfaa-4f71c8a3de36"}